# Line endings.
#
# The repository stores text as LF. Working copies get whatever the platform
# wants, so Windows checkouts still see CRLF without that reaching a commit.
# Before this file the tree held 2758 LF files, 1769 CRLF files and 314 with
# both inside a single file, and any editor that rewrote one produced a diff of
# the whole file that buried the real change.
#
# text=auto covers every file, including types nobody has added yet: git decides
# text or binary by content. Only the pins below need touching again, and only
# if some new file type has to keep one specific ending.

* text=auto

# Files a tool or platform requires to keep one specific ending wherever they
# are checked out.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.sln   text eol=crlf
